<Base
  lang="en"
  page="status"
  eyebrow="Features and limits"
  title="Current implementation"
  description="Available features, the checks applied and what remains to be completed."
>
  <p class="lede">
    Lanternina is a prototype used in one home. Its activity path includes approval, printing, page reading and continuation. Some functions remain incomplete, and installation in other homes still needs to be tried.
  </p>

  <h2>Available features</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>
      The panel lets the parent prepare ideas, approve activities and choose preferences and hours.
    </li>
    <li>
      The house shows instructions on displays, prints pages and starts a scan when a button is pressed.
    </li>
    <li>
      The system generates activities and pages, reads added marks and prepares continuations. The household clock manages help and the start of the ending.
    </li>
    <li>Reminders, pictures generated from the parent's themes and an image archive.</li>
    <li>
      Device job assignments, an activity log and a household service-usage limit.
    </li>
    <li>Each display has its own connection interval in Devices. It receives changes at its next connection; low-battery protection can extend the interval.</li>
    <li>The handheld camera saves photographs before starting Wi-Fi. Authenticated originals can be viewed, downloaded and deleted by the family. Offline delivery was tested on the installed camera; retries preserve the capture identifier.</li>
    <li>The hub chooses an assigned compatible camera or scanner for each return and retains that choice. Photographed sheets are compared with their originals; objects and constructions need no original. Uncertain or late photographs do not advance the activity.</li>
    <li>The parent can create and revoke email-bound portal invitations. An invited adolescent can submit, inspect and delete their own photographs. The hub retrieves pending uploads; receipt alone does not mean a model has interpreted them.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Checks</h2>
  <p>The parent approves the initial activity. Generated activities and continuations pass format and safety checks; continuations do not require a second approval. Reading pages requires cloud connectivity. Retained data and deletion options are described under <a href="/en/#memory">memory</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="camera-checks">Camera checks</h2>
  <p>Prototype trials verified battery-powered capture, light feedback, sleep and wake. A receiver-offline test verified that a photograph stays saved on the camera and is delivered when connectivity returns. These results apply to the tested assembly and firmware; they do not establish battery life or performance across lighting conditions.</p>
  <p><a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/firmware/camera/README.md`}>Measurements, configurations and test conditions.</a></p>

  <h2>Open implementation gaps</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <b>Camera trials.</b> The sheet-return path has automated tests. A complete activity with photographed handwriting, varied lighting, power-interruption tests and battery-life measurements remain open. Firmware and wiring changes require new physical trials.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>The button panel.</b> The current hardware has one button per display. It can start a scan when the current return uses a scanner, but cannot yet capture a multiple-choice response. It does not start a scan while the moment waits for a camera.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Memory visibility.</b> A complete view and scan gallery are missing. The optional temporary reading archive has a 14-day lifetime; photo archives, activity traces and profile observations follow separate retention and deletion paths.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Activity quality.</b> Building, drawing and investigating can have open outcomes. Checks do not establish comprehension or interest; automatic judges retain false positives. A trial with a person is still needed.
    </li>
    <li><b>Print failure and timing.</b> A failed print shows a message already written in the activity, but the alternative path without a sheet is not executed. Consecutive steps that collect no response advance without waiting for their declared durations.</li>
    <li>
      <b>Other homes.</b> A complete installation has been tried in only one home. Household-bound hub credentials and cross-family refusals have automated tests; provisioning multiple physical homes remains untested. Real invited-account registration and redemption also remain to be exercised.
    </li>
  </ul>

